WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560
I’m often asked how I create the
videos you see on NutritionFacts.org.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.360
It’s not just me,

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.400
it’s a whole team
of staff and volunteers

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.200
who help bring
the videos to life.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.280
It all starts with the research
and every round of new videos,

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:16.960
I read through
every issue

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.320
of every English-language
nutrition journal in the world

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:23.360
—so busy folks like
you don’t have to.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:24.960
And that’s just the
tip of the iceberg.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.720
More than 300,000 nutrition papers
are published every year

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:32.000
in the scientific medical
literature in general

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.760
—about 1,000
studies a day.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.120
I typically start with what
I call “anchor” articles.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:43.880
These are the new studies juicy
enough to center a video around.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:47.160
Papers that are
groundbreaking, practical,

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:50.535
with actionable information,
and engaging.

00:00:50.535 --> 00:00:53.360
Sometimes there’s
trailblazing new science

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:54.960
with hands-on implications,

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:58.560
but unless I can find a way to
make the information interesting—

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:02.720
by adding humor or intrigue,
or solving a mystery—

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:05.880
sometimes, sadly,
it just doesn’t make the cut.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:09.960
Once I have the anchor paper,
the real work begins:

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:13.080
performing a comprehensive search
of all the available literature

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:16.120
to place that particular
paper in context.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:18.520
We primarily use
PubMed.gov,

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.200
the database of the
National Library of Medicine,

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.320
but I have started dabbling with
AI search tools like Elicit.org.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:28.520
Of course, just because
something is published

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:32.040
in the peer-reviewed medical
literature doesn’t mean it’s true.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:36.000
There are studies funded by the
National Confectioners Association

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.120
that purport to find that
candy is just dandy,

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:43.400
so it always helps to take potential
funding bias into account.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:46.960
Our article retrieval volunteers
then help download all the articles

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:49.600
we need to read to
analyze and synthesize

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:53.480
the best available balance of
evidence into an annotated script.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.600
Once the scripting work is done,
every script is fact-checked,

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:00.680
then videos are created by the
amazing team at Avo Media.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:03.920
They’re then reviewed again
by eagle-eyed volunteers

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.960
and our fact-
checker and staff,

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:07.880
then are polished,
translated,

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:10.360
and prepped to share
with the world.

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:13.760
We’ve also just brought on
a couple of new researchers

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:17.760
to help update the oldest
videos on NutritionFacts.org.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:21.880
These videos are outdated,
a little embarrassing,

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:26.240
but the topics are still fresh and
there’s a lot more research available,

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:30.480
so they’ll be getting
an entirely new refresh.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:34.640
This is all possible
because of our supporters.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:36.000
Everything on the
website is free.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.409
There are no ads,
no corporate sponsorships.

00:02:38.409 --> 00:02:40.400
It’s strictly noncommercial,
I’m not selling anything.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.080
I just put it up as
a public service,

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.240
as a labor of love.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.960
If NutritionFacts.org has helped you
or your family in any way

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:53.320
and you’d like to do your part
to keep the site going strong,

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:56.080
please consider joining
the thousands of individuals

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:58.920
who support this important
work and make a donation

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:03.644
to the 501(c)(3) nonprofit
that is NutritionFacts.org.

